    "text": "To determine how many more acorns each squirrel needs to collect, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of acorns each squirrel needs to get through the winter.\n2. Determine how many more acorns each squirrel needs to collect by subtracting the number of acorns each squirrel has already collected from the total number of acorns each squirrel needs.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total number of acorns each squirrel needs.\nEach squirrel needs 130 acorns to get through the winter. Since there are 5 squirrels, the total number of acorns needed is:\n\\[ 130 \\times 5 = 650 \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine how many more acorns each squirrel needs to collect.\nThe total number of acorns collected by all squirrels is 575. Therefore, the number of additional acorns each squirrel needs to collect is:\n\\[ 650 - 575 = 75 \\]\n\nSo, each squirrel needs to collect \\(\\boxed{75}\\) more acorns.",
